 "notes": "Boundary of the shaded exclusion region in Fig. 7 (bothd.eps, vector-traced; calibration verified against Table I to <3% at all seven tabulated masses). The paper's 95%-CL upper limit on the model-independent two-photon coupling xi = (4/3)(E/N-1.92) from a null search for axion-decay line emission in clusters A2667 and A2390 (VIMOS IFU at VLT), mass window 4.5-7.7 eV. Converted to g_agamma via the paper's Eq. (3) lifetime tau = 6.8e24 s xi^-2 m_eV^-5 and Gamma(a->2gamma) = g^2 m^3/(64 pi), giving g = 1.395e-10 GeV^-1 * xi * m_eV. Spikes to the top of the plot frame (xi ~ 5e-2, capped at the frame) occur near the 5577A and 6300A night-sky lines where no useful limit exists; curve values there reflect the plotted frame boundary. Limit assumes thermal relic axion abundance Omega_a h^2 = m_eV/130 (not a local halo density), so no rho_DM rescaling applies.",
